__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
# Without the second line a `.venv` SYMLINK is not ignored: a trailing slash
# matches a directory only, and a sibling git worktree sharing one environment
# reaches it by symlink. One was committed that way -- mode 120000 holding an
# absolute path, which breaks every other checkout of the branch.
.venv
.pytest_cache/
.hypothesis/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
build/
*.egg-info/

# generated by docs/plan/render.py
docs/plan/*.html

# pytest report artifacts: a run is a dated measurement, not source.
test-results/

# the accepts corpus CACHE: drawn instances held between runs, keyed on the bundle document
# and pointer they were drawn for (tests/corpus.py).  The cache is a build artifact; the
# COMMITTED floor it starts from is tests/accepts-corpus/ and is tracked, because the key is
# the document's own bytes and no compiler edit moves it (docs/plan/architecture.md, "The
# drawn corpus is COMMITTED").  Only the cache is ever written by a run.
.accepts-corpus/

# Derived: tests/emitted.py's cross-process compile cache, keyed on the compiler's own
# source so a codegen edit moves the key.  Never committed -- a committed one is a file
# a reader could edit into a result no compiler produced.
.emit-cache/

# Both of the above once ADCP_CACHE points them inside a checkout: the default is beside
# the checkouts instead, so neither is normally here at all.  Ignored by NAME because the
# two stores are keyed on content and share one root across worktrees.
.adcp-cache/

# The suite's scratch: pytest's basetemp and every tempfile.mkdtemp, which tests/conftest.py
# points at a DISK path beside the checkout because /tmp here is a 63 GB tmpfs and a fresh
# package is 841 MB per tmp_path. Normally not here at all; ignored by name for the case
# ADCP_SCRATCH points it back inside a checkout, which is the same defence .adcp-cache has.
.adcp-scratch/
